Forked on 7 November 2026 by Affluent Labs LLC for ZestSSH. What came from vnc-rs stays under
its licence; our additions follow this crate's own licence (Cargo.toml) unless the fork
is published under vnc-rs's terms. What changed against vnc-rs 0.6.0:

  - Moved from a crate into a module (crate:: paths became crate::vnc::engine::); the wasm
    paths, the tracing logging (now silent no-op macros), and the futures, tokio-stream,
    tokio-util and async_io_stream dependencies were removed (a small channel reader replaces
    the bridge); thiserror 1 became thiserror 2.
  - New: connect() (client/connect.rs) with ConnectOptions and SessionInfo; security types
    VeNCrypt (client/vencrypt.rs: X509None, X509Vnc, X509Plain over rustls with ring, the
    certificate trusted by its SHA-256 pin only) and Apple Remote Desktop (client/ard.rs).
  - New encodings: RRE, Hextile, Zlib (codec/rre.rs); Tight's JPEG decoded (zune-jpeg); the
    JPEG quality and compression level pseudo encodings; QEMU extended key events; the
    extended clipboard (client/clipboard.rs, UTF-8).
  - New events: Rectangle (each rectangle's encoding), UpdateDone (the end of an update),
    QemuKeyEvents; new input: ScancodeKey. A layout-only answer before the first pixels is
    followed by another update request. Plain ServerCutText and ClientCutText are Latin-1, as
    RFC 6143 says (vnc-rs read them as UTF-8).
  - VncEncoding carries the level encodings' values; its wire numbers come from wire().
  - Later in the 4.0 work: continuous updates with fences, a pause (no requests, continuous
    updates off), close reasons with the stream's end, pixels drawn straight into the app's
    picture (DrawTarget), receiving without the lock input needs, limits on every size the
    server sends, TRLE read as RFC 6143 says (no length or zlib, 16-pixel tiles), and the
    credentials wiped from memory after the handshake.

No code was copied from GPL sources (TigerVNC, LibVNCClient, KasmVNC) or from RoyalVNC;
TigerVNC was only run, as a test server.
